## Registry import consistency (#229)

### Context
Registry import left renamed domains with stale namespaces, flipped auto
base URIs to the built-in host on Domain → General save, imported
Published copies as Published, and Overwrite replaced existing versions.
Ported from the 0.9.3 fix onto 0.10.0.

### Changes
1. `src/api/routers/internal/domain.py` — pass `settings` into `Domain` on save
2. `src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py` — raise when default base URI resolve fails
3. `src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py` — WARNING on global-config read failure
4. `src/back/objects/domain/settings/ObxSettings.py` — full URI rewrite on rename; skip existing versions; DRAFT highest new; extract helpers under size budget
5. `src/api/routers/internal/settings.py` — document `add_missing` / overwrite semantics
6. `src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js` — Add missing versions UI and skipped-version notice
7. `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/advanced_features.md` — import behaviour
8. `tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py`, `tests/units/settings/test_settings_obx.py`,
   `tests/units/settings/test_v090_settings_obx.py`, `tests/units/architecture/baseline.json`
   — coverage and size ratchet update

