## Use "Context" instead of "Domain" in the user-facing UI
================================================================================

Context: The Ontobricks concept was still labelled "Domain" in several places
the user reads (Registry popups, Settings, Context page, help modal, toasts,
confirm dialogs, API docs tags). The concept is now called "Context" in every
visible label, title, placeholder, notification and error message. Kept as-is
on purpose: code identifiers, routes (`/domain/...`), API parameters and
response keys (`domain_name`, `domains`), CSS classes, element ids, OWL
`rdfs:domain`, the Databricks Knowledge Pages `domain` attribute/filter, and
the LLM/MCP-facing prompts and tool descriptions (agent behaviour unchanged,
no eval impact).

Changes:
1. src/front/templates/** — visible text, titles, placeholders, aria-labels of
   the Context page, Registry (Bridges subtitle now reads "Cross-contexts
   bridges connecting ontology entities across contexts"), Settings, help
   modal, ontology/mapping panels, dtwin API docs, access-denied page.
2. src/front/static/**/*.js — notifications, confirm dialogs, tooltips,
   dropdown placeholders, loading overlays, Registry/Bridges/Teams labels.
3. src/api/**, src/back/**, src/front/routes/**, src/shared/** — HTTP error and
   validation messages, job progress labels, OpenAPI descriptions and tag names
   ("Domain" -> "Context", "List Contexts", ...). Log lines, docstrings and SQL
   left untouched.
4. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-pages.js and
   src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_pages.html — kept "Databricks
   Domain" wording for the Knowledge Pages filter (Databricks-side attribute).
5. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js, src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
   — fallback labels ("context") shown in the loading and switch dialogs.
6. src/shared/config/constants.py — no change (LLM wizard prompt kept as-is).
7. tests/** — assertions updated to the new wording (API messages, OpenAPI tag,
   UI strings, JS contract strings).

